# JetBrains. Untracked but not ignored is the dangerous combination: it puts local IDE
# state (including per-user paths and run configs) one `git add -A` away from a public
# repo, and it shows up as noise in every `git status` while reviewing.
.idea/

# Python Workers vendoring (broker/)
#
# `pywrangler sync` resolves the broker's dependencies against the Emscripten target and
# unpacks the wheels into python_modules/, rebuilt on every deploy. .venv-workers/ is the
# throwaway interpreter it resolves with. broker/pylock.toml IS committed: it pins the
# exact wheel set that gets bundled, which is the whole point.
python_modules/
.venv-workers/

